  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1135 AM CDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nThe remainder of the week remains hot, although not quite to the \nlevels we saw last week thanks to lower height, generally between\n5920 and 5950 meters at 500 mb. The zonal ridge axis begins to \nshow some weakness by Friday as the high's center retreats toward \nthe Great Basin, so this would allow for some cooler northerly \nflow aloft supportive of less capping and perhaps some late-day \nand overnight storms for parts of our area. Until then, the storm \nchances remain holed up in/near the Oklahoma Panhandle along a \nweak cold front that stalls out from Tuesday through Thursday.",
